Changes to OCCT (V8_0_1) for the 3D Viewer. Applied by wasm/scripts/build-occt.sh.

- STEP AP242: recognise draughting models that are also tessellated shape representations
  (complex instances with SHAPE_REPRESENTATION and TESSELLATED_SHAPE_REPRESENTATION, with or
  without CHARACTERIZED_OBJECT). OCCT skipped them, so PMI in them lost its length unit (inch
  PMI read as mm) and saved views attached to them were dropped. Seen in the NIST AP242 PMI files.
- STEP AP242 e3: read DRAUGHTING_MODEL_ITEM_ASSOCIATION_WITH_PLACEHOLDER as the association it
  extends (the placeholder is ignored). It links PMI to its presentation, so OCCT dropped the
  graphics of every dimension, tolerance and datum that used only it, and imported datum
  symbols as notes. Seen in the NIST e3 files (stc_06..08, stc_10, ctc_02, ctc_03, ftc_06).
  - readAnnotation skips associations to callouts holding only an annotation placeholder.
  - PMI presentations are read after semantic PMI. A presentation is not read again as a note
    when the semantic PMI already took it (this also drops duplicate notes in e1/e2 files),
    and the note path prefers an association to a plain shape aspect over one to the PMI.
- Datums take their faces from item_identified_representation_usage (not only
  geometric_item_specific_usage) on the datum, its features, or shape aspects the features
  relate to, and identified items given as a typed list, SET_REPRESENTATION_ITEM((...)), are
  read. Datums in the NIST files had no faces.
- Dimensions and tolerances take their shapes from item_identified_representation_usage too,
  and prefer it over a property definition on the same shape aspect (AP242 attaches semantic
  text there). OCCT dropped such PMI because it found no shapes.
- Dimensions without a value still read their presentation.
- A presentation whose PMI could not be read (an unsupported entity, e.g. a tolerance with a
  defined unit or area unit) is imported as a note, even when other PMI shares its shape aspect.
- STEP: read tolerances per unit length or area (a tolerance type with
  GEOMETRIC_TOLERANCE_WITH_DEFINED_UNIT and optionally _WITH_DEFINED_AREA_UNIT) as the new
  complex entity StepDimTol_GeoTolAndGeoTolWthDefUnit (type 827). XCAF tolerances get the unit
  size, second unit size and unit area shape (XCAFDimTolObjects_GeomToleranceUnitArea), stored
  under a new child label. OCCT read these as unknown entities and dropped them.
- Tolerances on the whole part find the B-rep through shape_representation_relationship when
  the part's shape representation is not the B-rep itself.

